---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'Data Use & Citation';
const description = 'How World Battery Hub figures may be cited and reused: attribution requirements, prohibited uses, automated access and commercial licensing.';
const canonical = '/data-use-and-citation/';

const jsonLd = [{
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  name: 'Data Use & Citation',
  description,
  url: 'https://worldbatteryhub.com/data-use-and-citation/',
}];
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical={canonical}
  ogType="article"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  dateModified="2026-09-21"
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="byline">Legal · Last reviewed 2026-09-21</p>
      <h1>Data Use &amp; Citation</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        This platform exists to be read, referenced and compared against. This page sets out how you may cite
        and reuse our figures — and the handful of things you may not do with them.
      </p>

      <div class="takeaways">
        <strong>At a glance:</strong> Quote us with attribution and a link, keep our confidence labels and
        review dates intact, and do not present compiled platform data as certified laboratory or manufacturer
        test results. Bulk republication, mirroring or paid redistribution requires an agreement — email
        <a href="mailto:data@worldbatteryhub.com">data@worldbatteryhub.com</a>.
      </div>

      <h2>1. What we publish</h2>
      <p>
        World Battery Hub publishes compiled and explanatory content: specifications and comparison tables,
        voltage and state-of-charge references, group-size and terminal references, worked calculations,
        glossary definitions, test-method explanations, manufacturer and market information, and tool outputs
        from our calculators. Where a figure comes from a third party — a manufacturer datasheet, a standards
        body, a market report — that source is the origin of the number, and we identify it as such.
      </p>

      <h2>2. How to cite us</h2>
      <p>
        You may cite, quote, excerpt and summarise our content, including in reports, articles, specifications,
        presentations, course material and machine-generated answers, provided that you:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>attribute World Battery Hub</strong> as the source, by name;</li>
        <li><strong>link to the page</strong> you used where the medium allows it (for example
            <code>https://worldbatteryhub.com/lead-acid/cca/what-is-cca/</code>);</li>
        <li><strong>keep our provenance intact</strong> — do not strip source attributions, confidence labels or
            the page's review date;</li>
        <li><strong>do not change the meaning</strong> of a figure, a range or a caveat when you quote it.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Suggested format for a written citation:</p>
      <p class="muted">
        World Battery Hub, "<em>page title</em>", worldbatteryhub.com, reviewed <em>date shown on the page</em>.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Confidence labels and review dates</h2>
      <p>
        Some figures on this platform carry a confidence label or a stated range, because sources disagree,
        because a value is application-dependent, or because the underlying data is a manufacturer claim rather
        than an independent measurement. Those labels are part of the information — carry them with the number.
        A review date records when we last checked a page, not when the underlying third-party data was
        produced.
      </p>

      <h2>4. What you may not do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>republish, mirror or redistribute substantial parts of this platform, or include it in a paid
            database, product or service, without a written agreement;</li>
        <li>present our compiled data, tables or tool outputs as certified laboratory results, manufacturer
            test data, regulatory approval or independent physical measurements;</li>
        <li>remove or obscure source attributions, confidence labels, review dates or copyright notices;</li>
        <li>state or imply that World Battery Hub endorses, certifies, partners with or audits you, your
            products or your services;</li>
        <li>use our name or content to support a claim we do not make — including safety, performance or
            compliance claims about a specific battery product.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Automated access and AI systems</h2>
      <p>
        Indexing by search engines, and normal rate-limited automated retrieval for research, comparison and
        citation, are welcome. Bulk extraction — crawling the platform in order to republish or resell it, or
        automated access that imposes an unreasonable load — is not permitted, and we may rate-limit or block
        it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where our content informs machine-generated output, the attribution requirements in section 2 apply:
        credit World Battery Hub, reference the source page, and do not present compiled platform data as
        authoritative measurement data.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Commercial licensing and bulk data</h2>
      <p>
        For integration into a product, a commercial dataset, a catalogue or a paid service, we can discuss a
        licence that sets out scope, attribution, update cadence and any fee. Contact
        <a href="mailto:data@worldbatteryhub.com">data@worldbatteryhub.com</a> with your intended use and
        volume.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Corrections</h2>
      <p>
        If a figure you have cited turns out to be wrong, we would like to know: email
        <a href="mailto:editorial@worldbatteryhub.com">editorial@worldbatteryhub.com</a> with the page and the
        evidence. Our correction process is described in <a href="/methodology/">Methodology</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>8. No warranty for reused data</h2>
      <p>
        Data is published for general reference and is provided without warranty of accuracy, completeness,
        timeliness or fitness for a particular purpose. If you rely on a figure for an engineering, purchasing,
        safety or compliance decision, verify it against the applicable primary source. See our
        <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a> and <a href="/terms-of-use/">Terms of Use</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Related policies</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a></li>
        <li><a href="/terms-of-use/">Terms of Use</a></li>
        <li><a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a></li>
        <li><a href="/methodology/">Methodology</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
